## 1. Architecture: how this repo uses LLMs

```text
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ HEALING-WEBHOOK (server-side, default no LLM)               │
│   alert → vallm syntax check → planfile ticket creation     │
│   • default: DOES NOT call OpenAI/OpenRouter directly       │
│   • opt-in: may call redsl improve when explicitly enabled  │
│   • produces an LLM-ready ticket with full context          │
└────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────┘
                             │ ticket: PLF-XXX
                             ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ WINDSURF AGENT (you, using Windsurf-native LLM)             │
│   • reads ticket via planfile                               │
│   • edits code with Windsurf model (no external API)        │
│   • runs validation: pytest, regix, redup, vallm            │
│   • commits with conventional message (goal commit)         │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

## 2. Standard workflow (90% case)

```bash
# 1. Highest-priority ticket
task tickets:next

# 2. Read ticket + affected files
task tickets:show -- PLF-XXX

# 3. Edit code (Windsurf-native LLM)

# 4. Self-validate (LLM-free)
task quality:regix:local       # 0 errors required
task test                      # all tests pass

# 5. Add regression test (no exceptions)

# 6. Commit (goal generates smart message)
goal commit

# 7. Mark done
task tickets:done -- PLF-XXX
```

## 3. Tools available

| Layer | Tools |
|---|---|
| **Detect** | `regix`, `redup`, `prefact`, `testql`, `planfile`, `vallm`, `sumd`, `op3` |
| **Resolve** | Windsurf LLM (you), `pfix`, `aider`, `redsl` (opt-in OpenRouter) |
| **Validate** | `ruff`, `pytest`, `regix`, `vallm` |
| **Orchestrate** | `goal` (commits), `doql` (state), `costs` (tracking) |

Per-tool docs: `docs/llm-tools/<tool>/README.md`.

## 4. When to stop and ask user

- Patch > 80 lines diff → split ticket
- Need to touch file outside "Likely-affected areas"
- Need to bump dependency version
- Need to disable a test (even temporarily)
- Reproduction fails for unclear reasons (3+ tries)
- Not 80% sure of intent → don't guess

Don't ask about:

- Type hints, docstrings, local variable renames
- Adding regression tests
- Running `task` / pytest / regix to verify
- Small in-method refactors

## 5. Anti-patterns (red flags)

❌ **No commit before:**

- `task quality:regix:local` (must be 0 errors)
- Regression test added
- `git status` shows only intended files

❌ **Don't `--no-verify`** to skip pre-commit. Fix the cause.

❌ **Don't call `redsl improve` / `llx fix` / `aider`** in normal ticket
flow. These are opt-in OpenRouter automation lane only.

❌ **Don't modify generated code:** `**/*_pb2*.py`, `**/__generated__/**`.

❌ **Don't `print()`** in production. Use `logging`.

❌ **Don't guess imports** — find real symbol in neighboring files.

## 6. Citation format

Use absolute paths in backticks:

```text
`@/path/to/repo/src/file.py:42-48`
```

Never plain text. Never relative paths in chat output.

